1	// The printer panel's choices, actions, and confirmation of a proposed change.
2	// Setup guidance lives in the conversation, without a pinned hardware summary.
3	//
4	// Everything here renders host state, in words made on this page
5	// (printerWords.ts). A tap sends a typed printer action or a tool decision,
6	// which C++ carries out -- never a change made on this side, and never words
7	// sent as the person's. A tap the model should know about carries its note,
8	// which the app records if the tap goes through.
